{"blocks":[["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/","source-block-263","Use Utility > Mic Settings to match the microphone input to your voice or an external modulator. The menu controls Mic Gain, Noise Gate, and Mic Detection.",["19.8. Global Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/","source-block-426","Auto Gain is the default and suits average use with the Vocoder Edition microphone. A lavalier microphone or external audio source may need manual gain.",["19.8. Global Vocoder settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/01%20Mic%20Levels/","source-block-207","19.8.1. Setting microphone levels",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/01%20Mic%20Levels/","source-block-245","When a vocoder preset is selected, the OLED VU animation shows the microphone input level: Low, Mid, or Skull. Aim for Mid; Skull indicates a level that can distort the vocoder output.",["19.8.1. Setting microphone levels"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/02%20Gain/","source-block-291","19.8.2. What is gain?",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/02%20Gain/","source-block-317","Microphone signals are usually quiet, around -30 dB to -70 dB, and need amplification. The MicroFreak preamp can reduce or amplify the signal with a gain setting from -12 dB to +59 dB. Negative settings reduce the input; positive settings amplify it.",["19.8.2. What is gain?"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/","source-block-296","19.8.3. How do you set gain?",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/","source-block-329","The useful gain depends on how loudly you sing or speak and your distance from the microphone.",["19.8.3. How do you set gain?"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/","source-block-427","Set the MicroFreak master volume to about 50%, then use a non-vocoder preset to establish an average listening level.",["19.8.3. How do you set gain?"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/","source-block-548","Select the Vocoder Oscillator. Open Utility > Mic Settings > Mic Gain with the Preset encoder. Mic Gain defaults to Auto; turn the encoder left to choose a manual level.",["19.8.3. How do you set gain?"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/","source-block-725","Hold a key and speak or sing while adjusting gain until the vocoder is loud enough without distortion. For chords, enable Paraphonic mode and check the level again. Leave headroom if your voice changes volume widely.",["19.8.3. How do you set gain?"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/01%20Noise%20Gate/","source-block-240","19.8.3.1. Noise Gate",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/01%20Noise%20Gate/","source-block-265","When the microphone signal is amplified, background sounds are amplified too. The Noise Gate ignores sounds below its threshold while allowing a louder voice through.",["19.8.3.1. Noise Gate"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/01%20Noise%20Gate/","source-block-435","Off disables the gate. The default threshold is -70 dB; the detailed setting description gives a range of -30 dB to -98 dB.",["19.8.3.1. Noise Gate"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-335","19.8.3.2. Mic detection",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-363","On is the default. The MicroFreak checks for a microphone whenever a vocoder preset is loaded or the Vocoder Oscillator is selected.",["19.8.3.2. Mic detection"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/02%20Mic%20Detection/","source-block-503","If no microphone is detected, the display warns “warning! mic needed”. The mic input is disabled until the next preset loads, and the vocoder filterbank is bypassed, leaving the raw Vocoder Oscillator sound.",["19.8.3.2. Mic detection"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-329","19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-371","An external audio source can modulate the vocoder, including a guitar, drum machine, phone, tablet, or Eurorack mixer. Match its output level to the MicroFreak input: these sources are usually much louder than a microphone.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-598","Approximate output levels: microphones -60 to -40 dBU; guitar -20 dBU; phones and tablets -7.78 dBU; Eurorack +13 dBU.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-720","Use a headphone/microphone splitter that connects the source to the mic contact of the MicroFreak’s 3.5 mm TRRS jack.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-843","Headphone/Microphone Splitter",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1268","CTIA/AHJ connector",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1714","Connect the device",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1739","Turn off the MicroFreak and gently remove the gooseneck microphone.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1811","Turn the external device’s output level all the way down to avoid clipping.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-1893","Plug the splitter into the MicroFreak headphone jack and the device signal into the splitter’s mic branch.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-2006","Turn on the MicroFreak.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-2034","Set Utility > Mic Settings > Mic Detection to Off and Mic Gain initially to -12 dB.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/","source-block-2130","Select a vocoder preset, hold a key, and slowly raise Mic Gain. If there is no sound, slowly raise the source device’s output level.",["19.8.3.3. Connecting external sources","Connect the device"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/Asset/01-Headphone-Microphone-Splitter/png/","source-block-57","01 Headphone Microphone Splitter",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/03%20Set%20Gain/03%20External%20Sources/Asset/02-CTIA-AHJ-Connector/png/","source-block-57","02 CTIA AHJ Connector",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/","source-block-269","19.8.4. MIDI Control Center",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/","source-block-301","The MIDI Control Center for macOS and Windows can move presets between the MicroFreak and a computer and change MicroFreak settings.",["19.8.4. MIDI Control Center"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-214","19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-257","The global Vocoder settings here match those in the MicroFreak Utility menu.",["19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-337","MIDI Control Center Vocoder settings",["19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/","source-block-657","The software is available from Arturia.",["19.8.4.1. MIDI Control Center settings"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/08%20Global%20Settings/04%20MIDI%20Control%20Center/01%20Settings/Asset/01-MIDI-Control-Center-Vocoder-Settings/png/","source-block-57","01 MIDI Control Center Vocoder Settings",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/09%20Package/","source-block-233","19.9. MicroFreak Vocoder Package content",[]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/09%20Package/","source-block-278","The Vocoder Edition package includes:",["19.9. MicroFreak Vocoder Package content"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/09%20Package/","source-block-319","A white MicroFreak case with a swan graphic on the center strip.",["19.9. MicroFreak Vocoder Package content","The Vocoder Edition package includes:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/09%20Package/","source-block-388","A gooseneck electret microphone with an adapter/splitter and an added headphone output.",["19.9. MicroFreak Vocoder Package content","The Vocoder Edition package includes:"]],["Microfreak/UG/19%20Appendix%20B%20Vocoder/09%20Package/","source-block-480","A leaflet describing the microphone base and gooseneck.",["19.9. MicroFreak Vocoder Package content","The Vocoder Edition package includes:"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-190","20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet",[]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-221","Preset",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-234","Shift + Preset Encoder",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-261","Quickly select the “A”, “a”, “0”, or “.” character range.",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset","Shift + Preset Encoder"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-340","Long press Save",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-360","Quick save.",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset","Long press Save"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-377","Press the Preset Encoder three times",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-418","Reset the current preset to its Init state.",["20 Appendix C: Cheat Sheet","Preset","Press the Preset Encoder three times"]],["Microfreak/UG/20%20Appendix%20C%20-%20Cheat%20Sheet/","source-block-467","Osc